# UI / UX Excellence

UI should feel premium, intentional, and memorable — not template-y or generic AI SaaS.

## Visual & interaction

- Strong hierarchy, spacing rhythm, and purposeful typography.
- Cohesive design tokens / CSS variables; pick a clear visual direction and commit.
- Motion: 2–3 intentional microinteractions that create presence — not noise.
- Mobile-first responsive; desktop should feel composed, not stretched.
- One clear primary action per view.
- Every screen: loading, empty, and error treatments that feel designed.

## Avoid generic AI looks (unless the product truly is that)

- Purple-on-white / purple→indigo gradient themes as a default
- Interchangeable card grids and stock dashboard chrome
- Warm cream + terracotta “AI startup” serif cliché as a default
- Pill clusters, stat strips, icon rows, and cluttered hero chrome
- Dark mode + glow effects as a lazy default

Align with existing Cursor frontend design user rules; do not contradict them.

## Composition reminders

- Brand/product name is a hero-level signal on branded surfaces.
- Prefer real visual anchors (product/context imagery) over pure abstract decoration when relevant.
- Cards only when they contain interaction; otherwise reduce chrome.

## DO / DON'T

- ✅ DO: Distinct type pairing, tokenized color/spacing, one signature motion
- ✅ DO: Empty state with a single strong CTA and helpful copy
- ❌ DON'T: Default Inter/Roboto/Arial stacks when expressive type fits
- ❌ DON'T: Flat single-color pages with no atmosphere or hierarchy
